Step one：Add sigmanoise parameters in ./source/fdist3d_class.f03
1、Define sigmanoise in fdist3d_001 tpye part
real::sigxnoise,sigynoise
2、Set sigmanoise in input part:init_fdist3d_001(this,input,i)
(1)Also define the sigmanoise
real::sigxnoise,sigynoise
(2)Set sigmanoise input format 
call input%get(trim(s1)//'.sigma_noise(1)',sigxnoise)
call input%get(trim(s1)//'.sigma_noise(2)',sigynoise)
this%sigxnoise = sigxnoise/dx
this%sigynoise = sigynoise/dy
so in the qpinput.json, we have "sigma_noise" : [0.1,0.0],
we should pay attention to the consistent of "this%" of the parameters input, 
if we set call input%get(trim(s1)//'.sigma_noise(1)',this%sigxnoise),sigxnoise will be always zero.
(3)Initialize sigmanoise we set in Initialization part:dist3d_001(this,part3d,npp,fd)
 also define the sigmanoise
 real, dimension(2) :: sigmanoise
 sigmanoise = (/this%sigxnoise,this%sigynoise/)
 call PRVDIST32_RAN_PFL(……,sigmanoise),…… point to other parameters.
 in this part we call PRVDIST32_RAN_PFL, so next we need to add sigmanoise in the file in which we set up this function


Step two：Set the initialization of sigmanoise in ./source/part3d_lib77.f
1、we need to clear the meaning of sigmanoise
sigmanoise: slice beam centroid with random distribution, actually we should add nosie in sigmax or sigmy parameters, 
but in quickpic quiet start is used to make beam symmetric, so before we add sigmanoise, we should set quiet start to false to save file,
and next add sigmanoise based on the file we saved.
2、define sigmanoise
real sigmanoise
dimension sigmanoise(0:1)
3、add tempnoise to change sigmanoise in the later
real tempnoisex,tempnoisey
4、add sigmanoise in sigmax or sigmy
(1)tempnoisex = sigmanoise(0)*ranorm()
tempnoisey = sigmanoise(1)*ranorm()
in quickpic, ranorm() means Gaussian distribution, also eques to N(0,1) distribution
(2)for quiet start
in profile 1, except for 1 particle, quickpic set 7 particles for quiet start , in other words, 8 particles are a group.
actulally, these 7 particles are getted through rotating partilce every 45°. 
so we need to change sigmanoise every 8 particle, in other words, every 8 partices have the same sigmanoise：
part(1,npt,m) = tempx + tempxx + tempnoisex
part(2,npt,m) = tempy + tempyy + tempnoisey


